      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has a room-temperature compressive yield strength of approximately 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has limited room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The limited ductility of equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo is caused by its high Mo content.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V has lower electronegativity than Mo.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V is more ductility-promoting than Mo in this alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing 10–20% of the Mo with V will reduce the alloy's overall electronegativity mismatch.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo with V will modify lattice distortion in the BCC solid solution.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V-modified alloy will retain a disordered BCC solid solution after melting and homogenization.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing electronegativity mismatch will diminish directional bonding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Diminished directional bonding will enhance dislocation mobility and make slip easier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced dislocation mobility will increase room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The remaining Mo and other refractory elements will preserve much of the alloy's strengthening contribution.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions",
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 10–20% substitution of Mo by V will produce at least a 10–15% increase in room-temperature compressive plastic strain relative to the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a 10–20% substitution of Mo by V, compressive yield strength will remain near 1719 MPa and at least approximately 1600 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing more than about 20% of the Mo may excessively reduce yield strength.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Processing history and microstructural homogeneity can influence the strength–plasticity response.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to improve plastic strain by at least 10–15%, or a yield-strength decrease below approximately 1600 MPa, will falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
